## Report
Built the debug test target (`cargo test -p server-core --no-run`). Added a targeted PoC test `object_read_denied_policy_can_be_bypassed_when_fast_path_is_stale` in `core_tests.rs` (lines 4896-4934) that: creates a bucket/object, warms the fast-path, installs an explicit deny policy, confirms `HeadObject` is denied when policy is present, then forces the fast-path cache to `bucket_policy_present=false` via `update_bucket_fast_path_if_present` and retries the read. Running `cargo test -p server-core object_read_denied_policy_can_be_bypassed_when_fast_path_is_stale -- --nocapture` panics with `expected AccessDenied with stale fast-path, got Ok(HeadObjectResult { ... size: 4 ... })`, showing the read succeeds despite the deny policy (test output in artifact). Code evidence: `load_bucket_handle_for_object_policy_read` returns early when fast-path says no policy (authz.rs:1673-1705), and `authorize_object_read` uses this loader (authz.rs:4517-4538). `cached_bucket_policy_for_loaded_handle` also short-circuits to `None` when `bucket_policy_present` is false (authz.rs:733-760), so the policy is never loaded. `put_bucket_policy` writes the policy then updates the fast-path cache (bucket.rs:764-789), creating the stale-cache window. Valgrind was not installed; ASan attempt failed due to non-nightly compiler. Debugger attempt used lldb to run the failing test (same panic, no stack since process exited).

# Resolution validation
- the generic object-read fast path used by the PoC has been removed for
  non-BOE buckets
- BOE reads now use a shared coordinator-layer cache keyed by complete fast-path
  entries rather than a summary with `bucket_policy_present == false`
- that cache is freshness-gated by persisted `bucket_execution_generation`
- stale or deleted entries reload or evict before they can authorize a BOE read
  as fresh

